curate, incomplete or outdated, even when it appears confident and detailed;</li>\n<li>actions the Agent performs may not work as you intended;</li>\n<li>you should independently verify Output before relying on it, and apply human judgment before acting on it;</li>\n<li>Output does not represent our views, and may occasionally include content you find incorrect or objectionable;</li>\n<li>the Service is not a substitute for advice from a qualified professional.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. Feedback</h3>\n<p>Feedback is one of the main goals of the pilot, and we appreciate it. If you send us feedback, suggestions or ideas, you agree that we may use them freely, without restriction and without compensation or attribution.</p>\n<h3>10. Third party services</h3>\n<p>The Service operates on top of third party services, including Telegram (the messaging platform through which you access the Agent), cloud hosting providers, and providers of AI models that power the Agent. In addition, some features may interact with external tools or websites at your request.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Third party services are governed by their own terms and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for them.</li>\n<li>We do not control Telegram; messages you send and receive through Telegram are also processed by Telegram under its own policies.</li>\n<li>If the Agent retrieves information from external sources at your request, we are not responsible for the content of those sources.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>11. Changes, suspension and discontinuation of the Service</h3>\n<p>This is a pilot. We may modify the Service, add or remove features, change usage limits, or suspend or discontinue the Service, in whole or in part, at any time. Where a change materially reduces the Service, we will make reasonable efforts to notify you in advance through the Agent or the contact details you provided. We are not liable for any modification, suspension or discontinuation of the Service, to the fullest extent permitted by law.</p>\n<h3>12. Termination</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>By you:</strong> you may stop using the Service and leave the pilot at any time, without notice and without giving a reason. You may also ask us to delete your data, as described in the Privacy Policy.</li>\n<li><strong>By us:</strong> we may suspend or terminate your access if we reasonably believe you have breached these Terms, if we are required to do so by law, or if it is necessary to protect the Service, other users or any third party. Where reasonably possible we will give you notice and an opportunity to respond before doing so.</li>\n<li>We may also terminate access as part of ending the pilot itself (section 2).</li>\n<li>Sections that by their nature should survive termination (including sections 8, 9, 13, 14, 15 and 17) will survive.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>13. Disclaimer of warranties</h3>\n<p>The Service, the Agent and all Output are provided on an \"AS IS\" and \"AS AVAILABLE\" basis, without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied or statutory, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law. Without limiting the above, we do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, timely, secure or error free, that Output will be accurate or reliable, or that any data or content will be preserved without loss. This is an experimental pilot, and parts of the Service may not function correctly or at all. Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits any right granted to you by applicable law that cannot be excluded or limited by agreement.</p>\n<h3>14. Limitation of liability</h3>\n<p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>we will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or exemplary damages, including loss of profits, loss of data, loss of goodwill or loss of business opportunity, arising out of or relating to the Service or these Terms, even if we were advised of the possibility of such damages;</li>\n<li>because the Service is provided free of charge and no fees are paid for it, our liability to you is limited to the maximum extent permitted by law.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These limitations do not apply to liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law. If applicable law does not allow a limitation above, that limitation will apply to the maximum extent permitted.</p>\n<h3>15. Indemnification</h3>\n<p>If a third party brings a claim against us that arises from your breach of these Terms or from your unlawful use of the Service, you agree to compensate us for damages, losses and reasonable expenses (including reasonable legal fees) that we actually incur as a direct result, to the extent caused by your breach and subject to any limitation under applicable law. This section does not apply to claims arising from our own breach of these Terms.</p>\n<h3>16. Changes to these Terms</h3>\n<p>We may update these Terms from time to time, for example to reflect changes in the Service, in the pilot, or in applicable law. If a change materially affects your rights, we will give you advance notice through the Agent or the contact details you provided, at least 7 days before it takes effect, unless a shorter period is required for legal or security reasons. If you continue to use the Service after a change takes effect, the updated Terms will apply. If you do not agree to a change, you may stop using the Service and ask us to delete your data.</p>\n<h3>17. Governing law and jurisdiction</h3>\n<p>These Terms and any dispute arising from them or from use of the Service are governed by the laws of the State of Israel, without regard to conflict of law rules. Subject to any mandatory law granting you a different forum, the competent courts in Tel Aviv Yafo will have exclusive jurisdiction. Nothing in this section limits rights available to you under mandatory consumer protection law.</p>\n<h3>18. General provisions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Entire agreement.</strong> These Terms and the Privacy Policy are the entire agreement between you and us regarding the pilot, and replace any prior understanding on this subject.</li>\n<li><strong>Severability.</strong> If any provision of these Terms is found invalid or unenforceable, it will be replaced by a valid provision that most closely reflects its intent, and the remaining provisions will remain in full force.</li>\n<li><strong>No waiver.</strong> A failure to enforce any provision is not a waiver of it.</li>\n<li><strong>Assignment.</strong> You may not assign your rights under these Terms. We may assign these Terms to an affiliate or to a successor of the activity, provided your rights are not reduced.</li>\n<li><strong>Language.</strong> These Terms are published in Hebrew and in English and are intended to be identical in substance. In case of inconsistency, the Hebrew version prevails.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>19. Contact</h3>\n<p>Questions about these Terms: elia@bencnaan.net</p>\n<h2>Privacy Policy</h2>\n<p>Effective date: July 27, 2026</p>\n<p>Data controller: NanoCo, contact: elia@bencnaan.net</p>\n<h3>1. Overview</h3>\n<p>This policy describes what information we collect during the pilot, how we use it, who can access it, and the choices you have. The short version: our analytics are based on behavioral data such as task types and usage patterns; our team does not read your conversations; we use data to improve the Service and for research and AI development; we do not sell data and we do not use it for advertising; and you can delete your data and your chat at any time.</p>\n<h3>2. What we collect</h3>\n<p><strong>Information you provide at registration:</strong> name, phone number and email address, as submitted in the signup form.</p>\n<p><strong>Conversation content:</strong> messages you send to the Agent and the responses it generates pass through our systems, because that is how the Service works. Content is processed automatically in order to respond to you and to operate the Service.</p>\n<p><strong>Behavioral and technical data:</strong> the types of tasks you ask the Agent to perform, usage patterns (for example frequency, times of use, session length and message counts), feature usage, error and performance events, and basic technical identifiers needed to route your messages (such as your Telegram user identifier).</p>\n<p><strong>What we do not collect:</strong> we do not collect payment information (the pilot is free), we do not use advertising trackers, and we do not purchase data about you from third parties.</p>\n<p>Please avoid sharing especially sensitive information with the Agent (for example medical, financial or biometric details about yourself or others) unless it is genuinely needed for a task you are asking it to perform.</p>\n<h3>3. How we use information</h3>\n<p>We use the information described above for the following purposes only:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Operating the Service:</strong> processing your messages so the Agent can respond and perform tasks, maintaining context, and providing support.</li>\n<li><strong>Optimization and improvement:</strong> understanding which kinds of tasks people use the Agent for and where it fails, so we can improve it. This analysis relies on behavioral data and aggregated statistics, not on reading personal content.</li>\n<li><strong>Research and AI development:</strong> studying usage of the pilot and developing our AI systems. These uses are noncommercial: we do not sell personal data, we do not share it for advertising, and we do not use it to target you with marketing.</li>\n<li><strong>Safety and security:</strong> preventing abuse, enforcing the Terms, and protecting the Service and its users.</li>\n<li><strong>Communicating with you:</strong> messages about the pilot itself, such as onboarding, changes and ending of the pilot.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Who can see your information</h3>\n<p>The Service is designed so that people are not routinely exposed to your personal content:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>We do not read your conversations as a routine practice. Analytics, research and product decisions rely on behavioral data and aggregated statistics, not on reading individual chats.</li>\n<li>Your personal content is not published, sold or exposed to third parties outside the systems that operate the Service.</li>\n<li>Access to raw content is technically restricted, and our team will access specific content only in limited cases: to debug or troubleshoot a technical problem with the Service, if you ask us to (for example a support request about a specific conversation), if we are required to by law, or if it is strictly necessary to investigate abuse or a security incident. Any such access is limited to what is necessary for that purpose.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Sharing and processors</h3>\n<p>We do not sell personal information and we do not share it for advertising. Information is shared only with service providers that are needed to operate the Service, and only for that purpose:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Telegram:</strong> your messages pass through Telegram, which processes them under its own privacy policy.</li>\n<li><strong>AI model providers:</strong> conversation content is processed by third party AI models in order to generate the Agent's responses, under agreements that restrict use of the data.</li>\n<li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure providers:</strong> servers and storage on which the Service runs.</li>\n<li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> we may disclose information if required by law, court order or a competent authority, or to protect legal rights in a dispute.</li>\n<li><strong>Corporate change:</strong> if the activity is transferred to another entity (for example merger or acquisition), data may be transferred with it, subject to this policy.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Some providers process data on servers located outside Israel. Where that is the case, transfer is carried out in accordance with the Privacy Protection Regulations (Transfer of Data to Databases Abroad), 2001.</p>\n<h3>6. Retention and deletion</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>During the pilot:</strong> we keep your data for as long as you participate.</li>\n<li><strong>Deletion on request:</strong> you can delete your chat and ask us to delete your data at any time, by asking the Agent or by writing to elia@bencnaan.net. We will complete deletion from our active systems within 30 days, except for minimal records we are required to keep by law or that are needed to resolve an open dispute.</li>\n<li><strong>After the pilot ends:</strong> personal data collected during the pilot will be deleted or anonymized within 90 days after the pilot ends, unless you have asked us to keep in touch about future versions.</li>\n<li><strong>Aggregated data:</strong> statistics that do not identify anyone (for example \"how many users asked for scheduling tasks\") may be retained and used after deletion.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>7. Your rights</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Voluntary provision:</strong> you are under no legal duty to provide us any information. Providing it depends on your consent. If you choose not to provide the registration details, we will not be able to include you in the pilot; that is the only consequence.</li>\n<li><strong>Access and correction:</strong> under the Israeli Privacy Protection Law, 1981, you have the right to review information about you held in our database and to request correction or deletion of information that is inaccurate, incomplete or outdated. To exercise these rights, write to elia@bencnaan.net.</li>\n<li><strong>Deletion and exit:</strong> as described in section 6, you can delete your data and leave the pilot at any time.</li>\n<li><strong>Complaints:</strong> you may also contact the Israeli Privacy Protection Authority.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>8. Security</h3>\n<p>We apply technical and organizational measures appropriate to a pilot of this kind to protect data from loss, misuse and unauthorized access, including access controls and encryption in transit. No internet service can be completely secure, so please use judgment about what you share.</p>\n<h3>9. Age</h3>\n<p>The Service is intended for adults aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect information from minors. If you believe a minor has provided us information, contact us at elia@bencnaan.net and we will delete it.</p>\n<h3>10. Changes to this policy</h3>\n<p>We may update this policy from time to time. If a change materially affects how we handle your personal information, we will notify you in advance through the Agent or the contact details you provided. The current version will always be available where the pilot documents are published.</p>\n<h3>11. Contact and controller details</h3>\n<p>The data controller is NanoCo. For any question, request or complaint regarding privacy: elia@bencnaan.net.</p>\n<hr></div>\n    <div class=\"foot\">Joni · NanoCo</div>\n  </div>\n<script>\nfunction setLang(l){\n  const he=l==='he';\n  document.getElementById('pane-he').classList.toggle('active',he);\n  document.getElementById('pane-en').classList.toggle('active',!he);\n  document.getElementById('btn-he').classList.toggle('active',he);\n  document.getElementById('btn-en').classList.toggle('active',!he);\n  document.documentElement.lang=l;\n  document.documentElement.dir=he?'rtl':'ltr';\n  window.scrollTo(0,0);\n}\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>","numLines":399,"startLine":1,"totalLines":399}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9aa1db45-d71c-450e-9940-41d81731dff3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"6ea58b35-88af-492f-a66a-95d96bc10fc6","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wobbly-cuddling-shell"}
