{"parentUuid":"91c013ae-de80-4249-89fb-2c63736bb04e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cddvwqdi6RBDDuiquGPjK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013zGFAURT9CUW7jycfCyJDF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/migration_runbook_aug2.md","content":"# NanoClaw Migration Runbook — old VM → new server (Aug 2 2026)\n\n**Deadline:** Gabi cuts access to the old VM (daniela.exe.xyz) **Thursday**. Cutover must be DONE + verified before then; old VM kept as rollback only until the cut.\n**Executor:** the dev agent (SSH/host access). **Coordinator/QA:** Daniela (ncl + HTTP verification). **Elia:** buys server, closes Pavel, hands SSH keys.\n\n---\n\n## GATES (nothing starts until these are true)\n- **G1 — Pavel:** NanoClaw engine is his closed-source. Confirm we may self-host AND get the deploy artifacts / source needed to stand it up on our own box. If he migrates it himself, this whole runbook is his; we only supply data.\n- **G2 — Server bought:** Netcup RS4000 (start) — order TODAY (new-account fraud-review can take 1–2 days).\n- **G3 — SSH keys:** to the new server, handed to the executor.\n\n## What must move (inventory)\n- **NanoClaw core** (Pavel's runner + `ncl` CLI + poll-loop) — needs G1 artifacts.\n- **Docker** — agents run in per-group containers.\n- **`data/v2.db`** (SQLite) — agent_groups, sessions, wirings, messaging-groups, destinations, users, roles.\n- **`groups/`** — every agent's workspace (memory, conversations, CLAUDE.local.md, mounted script sources).\n- **WhatsApp session store** (Baileys auth state) — losing it = re-pair the number.\n- **`.env`** — incl. **`ONECLI_BIND_HOST=172.17.0.1`** (wrong value kills every container), CONTAINER_MEMORY_LIMIT, MAX_CONCURRENT_CONTAINERS, fallback-provider keys, bot tokens.\n- **Tunnel config** — provision.shellano.com / provision.click2agent.com → currently point at old VM. Must re-point to new server.\n- **Telegram bot** `joni_agent_bot` — token; **single-instance** (see constraints).\n\n## HARD CONSTRAINTS (bake into every phase)\n1. **Single-instance bot** — never two NanoClaw instances polling `joni_agent_bot` at once → duplicated/broken inbound. **Old must STOP before new STARTS.**\n2. **ONECLI_BIND_HOST = 172.17.0.1** on the new box or containers die on boot.\n3. **Delta is live** — DB + groups + WhatsApp session change continuously while agents run. The T0 backup is stale by cutover; a final delta-sync happens inside the stop window.\n4. **No manual double-launch** of the pilot service.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1 — BACKUP (do first, TODAY, independent of Pavel & new server)\nThe insurance. Run on the old VM, from the NanoClaw root:\n```\ntar czf nanoclaw-backup-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M).tar.gz \\\n  data/v2.db groups/ .env \\\n  <whatsapp-session-dir> <tunnel-config-dir>\n```\nThen **download the tarball off the VM** (scp / rsync to a machine we keep). A backup that only lives on the VM being cut is not a backup.\nVerify: `tar tzf <file> | head` shows v2.db + groups/ + .env present; note the byte size.\n\n## PHASE 2 — PROVISION NEW BOX (after G2+G3)\n- OS + Docker + node/pnpm toolchain to match old VM versions.\n- Copy `.env` — **set `ONECLI_BIND_HOST=172.17.0.1`**, keep bot tokens, fallback keys, memory/concurrency limits.\n- Install NanoClaw core from Pavel's artifacts (G1). Do **not** start the poll-loop yet.\n\n## PHASE 3 — TEST WITHOUT TOUCHING THE LIVE BOT\n- Restore the T0 backup (v2.db + groups/ + WhatsApp session) onto the new box.\n- Bring up Docker + one test agent container against a **throwaway** bot token (never joni_agent_bot).\n- Verify: container boots, ncl sees the DB, an agent answers, WhatsApp session loads without re-pair.\n- Fix anything here — this is the safe window.\n\n## PHASE 4 — CUTOVER (atomic, inside a short stop window)\nOrder is mandatory (single-instance rule):\n1. **Announce** brief maintenance if needed.\n2. **STOP old** poll-loop (old instance no longer polls the bot).\n3. **Delta-sync** the live files old→new: v2.db, groups/, WhatsApp session (rsync the diff since T0).\n4. **Re-point tunnels** provision.shellano.com / provision.click2agent.com → new server IP.\n5. **START new** poll-loop on joni_agent_bot.\n6. Old VM stays powered (read-only fallback) until Gabi's cut.\n\n## PHASE 5 — VERIFY + ROLLBACK\nVerify (real commands, not assumptions):\n- `ncl groups list` / `ncl sessions list` on new box = full fleet present.\n- Send a Telegram test to joni_agent_bot → a pilot answers.\n- WhatsApp round-trip on 0548284911.\n- Tunnel: a real provision hit reaches the new box.\n- Boards still load (Vercel is external, unaffected).\n**Rollback** (if verify fails, before Gabi's cut): STOP new, re-point tunnels back, START old. Because we only delta-synced (never deleted old), old is intact.\n\n---\n\n## Ownership split\n- **Dev agent** (has SSH/host): Phases 1–4 execution, Docker, tar/rsync, tunnel re-point.\n- **Daniela** (ncl + HTTP): Phase 5 verification, ncl fleet checks, board checks, QA sign-off; standing by during cutover.\n- **Elia**: G1 (Pavel answer + artifacts), G2 (buy Netcup today), G3 (SSH keys to dev agent).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19771,"cache_read_input_tokens":44113,"output_tokens":3235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19771,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1310,"output_tokens":3235,"cache_read_input_tokens":44113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19771,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19771},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CddvwpHM6SdaiCw18B1Kc","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1159156-bf98-441f-8989-6232316c9e5c","timestamp":"2026